  "findings": [
    "Upper Hoback Highway189–Granite Creek now has an approximate public access map. Granite Creek is a takeout here, not a confirmed designated launch; all sections launching there remain held.",
    "Generic Tongue downstream-of-I90 identity resolved to Welch Ranch without changing the stable ID or source coordinate. Long Dayton-area float remains held; mandatory downstream diversion portage is now explicit.",
    "Three Snake course overviews reviewed completely and added for display only.",
    "Hoback trial course cuts a wooded bend and Prichard–Elbow source forks follow old island channels; both remain research only.",
    "Buck Creek public road approach remains unconfirmed; failed historical report download is not treated as present-day access authority."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Local only; no publication.",
    "No existing verified coordinates, stable IDs, planning miles, gauge assignments, speed calibrations or GPS features changed.",
    "No new precise landing, bank side, boat-carry connector or portage geometry adopted."
  ]
}
